  "prefLabel": "Eth 209.01 Role of Complainants and Committee Staff in Hearings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Eth 209.01 Role of Complainants and Committee Staff in Hearings.\n\n(a) Unless called as a witness or granted intervenor status, a complainant shall have no role in a hearing on the complaint conducted by the committee.\n\n(b) The investigator or other person designated by the attorney general shall present the case against the respondent to the committee.\n\nSource. #12617-A, eff 9-6-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/eth100-200.html"
